00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:53.910
Outaki?

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.130
Yes, hello.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:59.960
I'm calling to ask a question regarding Rodan.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.420
Oh, Outaki Factory! I just saw you guys on TV!

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.560
I gotta say, that was splendid work!

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:11.130
The Rodan previously had a strong reaction to this song.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.170
Why did you lure them in?

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.920
Lure them?

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.300
You are misunderstanding.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.930
The signal was an accident, or rather, more of an error.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:21.680
It was hardly intentional.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.500
So you claim they were inadvertently 
summoned due to some accident?

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:30.310
I suppose that's the case.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:37.490
We have assigned the name "red dust" 
to the red sand found on the Rodan.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:43.650
Possessing active and inactive states, it is 
a group of molecules that have complex structure.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.710
And its effects on us humans?

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:51.170
No reactions have been observed between the dust
 and the metabolism of the common organisms.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.550
Did it react to the Rodan's tissue?

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:57.930
Its connection to the red dust demands further research.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.970
Do you think there will be more of these 
giant creatures visiting us soon?

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:07.440
For example, a wingless terrestrial 
creature that walks on four—or even two legs.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:10.650
There is no basis for such assumptions at this stage.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.280
