00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:39.950
We were able to confirm a 
very interesting property of Archetype.

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:51.500
For instance, it can trap light.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:03.590
The trapped energy then increases.

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:08.250
The intensity of light should 
remain the same in a closed system...

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:24.070
The mystery behind this mechanism that seemingly defies the 
law of conservation of energy has not yet been understood.

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:27.890
When the system's energy increases, 
the light transfers more heat.

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:31.650
What if the light refracts 
beyond spatial dimensions?

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:37.070
This molecule that has only existed 
within simulations is now in our hands.

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:38.080
It's time!

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:41.370
If the light refracts through time,

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:46.700
and we consider it bringing scattered light with it, 
then photons could continuously materialize in one location!

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:52.540
In other words, photons that should appear in the future 
might all be appearing in advance at that one spot...

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:03.700
...is what I think.

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:09.230
You are Kamino Mei, yes?

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:10.240
What?

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:13.190
Y-Yes. Nice to meet you.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:15.440
Who on Earth?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.830
Thank you for your patience.

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:31.750
Welcome to B-150—the women's apparel department.

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:35.420
The bargain sale is on in the middle of the event hall.

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:40.220
We are expecting a large crowd so 
please watch your step while you shop.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.450
I sure hope I can pay by card.

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.810
The search team have arrived at the 2nd wall.

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:53.100
Intermittent tremors are continuing.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:54.100
How about the visuals?

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.870
We haven't gotten one since the brief image 24 hours ago.

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:22.130
Six years is just about enough time 
to finally unveil the iron maiden.

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:34.520
Please take the stairs ahead to the 
food court as the elevator is broken.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:47.630
The stairs are slippery so please watch your step!

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:54.390
How strange.

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:57.210
The foreleg suggests a plantigrade, 
and the hind leg a digitigrade?

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:58.920
Could there be two of them?

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:00.130
Plantigrade?

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:03.340
Plantigrades are species that walk
on the soles of their feet on the ground.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:04.970
Bears and humans, for example.

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.890
Digitigrades are species that only 
walk on their toes. Like horses and cats.

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:09.460
Maybe it's a chimera.

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:13.020
Doesn't seem like the Rodan came back to life.

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:15.640
Something came to hunt down its carcass.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:19.650
Are there any large animals in this area?

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:20.980
The naumann elephant?

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.070
They're 20,000 years too late.

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:35.850
Do elephants... eat birds?

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:38.580
Hey, lend me a hand!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.480
Alright! I'm on the way!

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:42.550
My apologies for rushing you.

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:44.090
Did you come straight from the airport?

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:46.300
Yes! Um...

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:46.300
Li!

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:51.060
Mei, this is Michael Steven.

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:55.020
You're that girl from before.

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:57.350
Tilda has dispatched a search group on her own.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:59.060
To the lake? Who?

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.270
She sent in BB!

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:02.630
They pulled this stunt while we were away.

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:05.820
I'm in the middle of business. Tell me lat—

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:07.550
I don't know the details!

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:09.360
We already discussed that case, didn't we?

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.070
Why won't she pick up her phone!?

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:13.110
That doesn't matter!

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:15.310
It seems I was right to call for you.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:17.990
Li! Come here a sec.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:22.670
I want to hear more about your "time" angle.

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.300
Can you write a report about it?

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:25.260
Okay!

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:26.840
Well, please have it ready by tomorrow.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:28.640
Huh? Um...

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:31.600
Listen, we won't make any progress from here.

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:34.470
When was the last time a person went in there?

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:34.120
By tomorrow...

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:38.720
It already got out from the river there.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:41.790
And before long, it had already 
gone back into the river, and then...

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:43.480
It jumped there.

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:44.610
What a mess.

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:47.490
All this back and forth... is it a young one?

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:50.990
If so, these random movements make more sense.

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:53.160
It must be a newcomer to this world.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:54.370
A newcomer this big?

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:57.080
Doesn't make a difference if it has a bigger parent.

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:00.330
It jumped from here.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.550
That's a 10-meter jump right there.

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:07.010
Hey!

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:09.900
You guys are following the footprints too?

00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:21.100
O-Ow...

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:23.310
Hey there.

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:25.360
Kai Takehiro.

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:27.190
A self-employed journalist.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:30.200
You guys sure seem familiar...

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:31.580
Oh, I remember!

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:34.280
You two are connected with
 that robot that defeated Rodan.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:35.410
There!

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:38.170
Footprints discovered!

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:40.640
C'mon, over here!

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:43.340
Isn't he chipper?

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:48.670
To think a temporary short-term researcher 
deserves this treatment.

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:49.800
Huh?

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:51.510
Where'd I put my key?

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:53.300
Right after I put it in my pocket, I...

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:55.900
You undressed and then put it inside your suitcase!

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:59.200
Hm. Makes sense.

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:01.810
Which came first? The chicken or the egg?

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:04.030
Isn't that example a bit weird?

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:08.820
Not only do I have a suitcase to open 
and a report to write by tomorrow,

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:10.710
but I also have that quiz I can't solve.

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:12.660
What's wrong?

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:16.530
You shouldn't be able to 
lock this suitcase without the key.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:19.160
Then how did you lock the key inside?

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.490
Maybe...

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:26.040
I see. It wasn't locked to begin with.

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:27.300
To begin with?

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:31.050
"Solve it and it'll make sense."

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:33.480
Ding dong! That's correct!

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.490
"Solve it and it'll make sense" is the answer!

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:41.830
It matches with the character string 
that Arikawa Yun sent you!

